  "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In triangles <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper D upper E upper F\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>D</mi>\n\t<mi>E</mi>\n\t<mi>F</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, angles <math alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper E\"><mi>E</mi>\n</math> each have measure <math alttext=\"27 degree\"><mrow><mn>27</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and angles <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> each have measure <math alttext=\"41 degree\"><mrow><mn>41</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Which additional piece of information is sufficient to determine whether triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is congruent to triangle <math alttext=\"upper D upper E upper F\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>D</mi>\n\t<mi>E</mi>\n\t<mi>F</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>?</p>",
